  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Budget Partnership Work Programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To increase budget transparency, accountability and participation in order to facilitate the achievement of the key development goals DFID is committed to. Increased transparency is now appreciated to be an essential component of development conditions that enable open economies and open societies to thrive. Improved budget transparency, accountability and participation will be achieved by providing the International Budget Partnership (IBP) with core funding for their 5 year programme. The expected outcomes of the IBP&#x2019;s work are: a) more transparent budget processes: timely, accessible, useful budget information is available to citizens and Civil Society Organisations (CSOs), b) CSOs analyse and participate in government budget processes, and work with formal oversight institutions to hold government to account, c) international policy community actively promotes budget transparency, participation, and accountability.</narrative>
  </description>
